 "description": "All fifteen implemented ViewTimeWin executions (ords 2-16) replayed per pinned module under the virtual clock: plain sliding #time expiry lifecycles with listener and iterator observation (just-select-star), windowed sum aggregates ungrouped/grouped/filtered over 30 ms windows with the quiet 35 s expiry, calendar-month rstream expiry (Feb/Mar 2002 quiet-at-minus-1ms boundary), the prev family over a sliding 1 s window, prepared-statement and variable window durations deployed twice (4 s vs 3 s) with rstream expiry at 4 s and 3 s, seven verbatim time-period spellings each equal to 30000 s observed across the 29999 s quiet boundary and the 30000 s expiry, and four flip-timer variants including calendar-month boundaries at epoch and 2002 start times. ord 12 splits into seven per-spec cases because the module resets advanceTime(0) per iteration and the Go clock never moves backwards.",
